{"title":"2014 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 15","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><dl><dd><i>The following problem is from the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12A_Problems\" title=\"2014 AMC 12A Problems\">2014 AMC 12A #11</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Problems\" title=\"2014 AMC 10A Problems\">2014 AMC 10A #15</a>, so those problems redirect to this page.</i></dd></dl>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Answer_Choices)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Answer Choices)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solutions\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solutions</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>David drives from his home to the airport to catch a flight.  He drives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/7/8c7f6c79f2148f0cec592c9517b40ee1b82ef22e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$35$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> miles in the first hour, but realizes that he will be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> hour late if he continues at this speed.  He increases his speed by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/9/f1965fae079a9ba2c0726c307070c2355dfcb213.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> miles per hour for the rest of the way to the airport and arrives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/1/651ba418a810d971dbc8a326d49a71fe1541fae0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> minutes early.  How many miles is the airport from his home?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/b/a5b439a33fc815980f4c254f1391b80f458db5b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) }140\\qquad \\textbf{(B) }175\\qquad \\textbf{(C) }210\\qquad \\textbf{(D) }245\\qquad \\textbf{(E) }280\\qquad$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"479\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note that he drives at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/6/906734e2f1010e9a171ffee8050cbc0649cea37c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$50$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> miles per hour after the first hour and continues doing so until he arrives.\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> be the distance still needed to travel after <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> hour. We have that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/1/a9127b3a2da512577645cc96eefb074c8db19732.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{d}{50}+1.5=\\dfrac{d}{35}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"116\" height=\"39\" />, where the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/7/15788e198a53ced87268aea78fcde68a84de92c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1.5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"25\" height=\"14\" /> comes from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> hour late decreased to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/2/192b4a258ee998961a99523fd0f0a029f9ea194a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0.5$\" width=\"22\" height=\"12\" /> hours early.\n</p><p>Simplifying gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/b/85bf40351ff84d8a1c9f735c4a5118a69884d5aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7d+525=10d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"120\" height=\"14\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/9/d698b8565da4feee5af744c1937ec518087e9387.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d=175$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p>Now, we must add an extra <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/7/8c7f6c79f2148f0cec592c9517b40ee1b82ef22e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$35$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> miles traveled in the first hour, giving a total of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/7/0d74cf7d99446217735b58e414f4f8f94203d4ce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C) } 210}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"75\" height=\"30\" /> miles.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Answer_Choices.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Answer_Choices)\">Solution 2 (Answer Choices)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Answer Choices)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Instead of spending time thinking about how one can set up an equation to solve the problem, one can simply start checking the answer choices.\nQuickly checking, we know that neither choice <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/6/a46f6af01fcf3bb5f6cac2316bc4de9bb3906bec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" /> or choice <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/1/b7193f66028e13f331d53ff5e6942c4b05587465.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(B)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> work, but <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/9/169b8d69bd74a91e72ec43123070d770633a340a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(C)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> does. We can verify as follows. After <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> hour at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/4/09466e152f1f4be5d8cbe343766bcae8ad1d2b55.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$35 \\text{ mph}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"55\" height=\"15\" />, David has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/a/caa2c5db610c6d7c961d76200b986305e4f13db0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$175$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" /> miles left. This then takes him <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/b/87b8245e043508c7c928c89b42f9ce38f04d720d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3.5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"25\" height=\"14\" /> hours at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/4/534b5f9b8fd7d547cc83168d73a540c5c0fe5779.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$50 \\text{ mph}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"55\" height=\"15\" />. But <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/6/6c60df89d196f27c4bdc994df5627998fa5dd235.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$210/35 = 6 \\text{ hours}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"132\" height=\"18\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/3/cc3b3f7c624ba241ff2b2a0acff93b695c494c92.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1+3.5 = 4.5 \\text{ hours}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"146\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/7/15788e198a53ced87268aea78fcde68a84de92c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1.5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"25\" height=\"14\" /> hours less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/f/57f9e1b3d108097fb959b943f8ac2653ca571135.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C)} \\: 210}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"73\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let the total distance be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and let the time taken after the speed change be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/d/e0d2bf360290fd61d1c1557e763f2622363b3d35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"13\" />. \nThen <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/9/479e9b262442bd3b8d4fce0097589547f833eef8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d=35(t+1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"106\" height=\"20\" />. Since 1 hour has passed, and he increased his speed by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/9/f1965fae079a9ba2c0726c307070c2355dfcb213.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> miles per hour, and he had already traveled <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/7/8c7f6c79f2148f0cec592c9517b40ee1b82ef22e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$35$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> miles, the new equation is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/2/00201b9c881e6f09d463160936e272925f7a1eac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d-35=50(t-1-\\frac{1}{2})=50(t-\\frac{3}{2})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"280\" height=\"38\" />. Solving, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/3/2e3ffb313a01c28f8b79b63e8c88e5f71704bc72.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d=35t+35=50t-40$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"190\" height=\"16\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/e/71ef5234ef6f8af1a146f507fb76a9802c4556c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15t=75$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"66\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/8/7a8e7bdfca7acbee99b041e26804dfb90a8a6737.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t=5$\" width=\"39\" height=\"12\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/2/6e2a76e178dd4ae3046d478cebae8edba6f20967.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d=35(5+1)=35\\cdot 6=210 \\Longrightarrow \\boxed{\\textbf{(C) } 210}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"337\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~JH. L\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solutions\">Video Solutions</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solutions\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>i) (<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/FyOhLdpeBLM?si=OY741QZ_WKpPMSDN\">https://youtu.be/FyOhLdpeBLM?si=OY741QZ_WKpPMSDN</a>)  [By WhyMath]\n</p><p>ii) (<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/UcE9-Hc3S9s?si=cuR-qhCD4Kn3D3sJ\">https://youtu.be/UcE9-Hc3S9s?si=cuR-qhCD4Kn3D3sJ</a>) [By Forbest Academy]\n</p><p>iii) (<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/eO6j_BQDyA4?si=mZg3B9pnqVjYfiP1\">https://youtu.be/eO6j_BQDyA4?si=mZg3B9pnqVjYfiP1</a>) [By Ashley Shen (in Chinese)]\n</p><p>~helloall35AAD\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A\" title=\"2014 AMC 10A\">2014 AMC 10A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Problems\" title=\"2014 AMC 10A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2014 AMC 10A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2014 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 14\">Problem 14</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2014 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 16\">Problem 16</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2014 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2014 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2014 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2014 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2014 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2014 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2014 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2014 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2014 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2014 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2